{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Both endpoints of this trip were amended after booking: the trip_record shows pickup_amended_at 2026-07-20T07:12:30 moving the pickup to Punggol MRT, and dropoff_amended_at 2026-07-20T07:41:52 moving the destination to Changi Terminal 3, with amended_optimal_distance_km 24.6 and amended_optimal_duration_min 31.0 both non-null. POL-RD-05 therefore requires POL-RD-01 to be re-applied against the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints, not against the booked 21.0 km Rivervale-to-T1 route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Measured against the amended optimal of 24.6 km, the governing trace distance of 26.17 km leaves an excess of about 1.57 km, which is roughly 6.4% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH limbs to pass - the excess must exceed 20% of optimal AND exceed 0.8 km absolute - and the percentage limb fails by a wide margin. No deviation survives the POL-RD-05 recomputation, and POL-RD-01 states that where either establishment test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The relocation POL-RD-05 keys on was the rider's own doing, and her own messages say so: 'im at punggol mrt phv pickup bay instead, moved the pin' at 07:11:58, and 'sorry ah can change to T3? my friend flight is T3 not T1' at 07:41:40, to which the driver replied 'ok changing now'. The extra distance is the direct consequence of the rider's two endpoint changes, not of any unilateral detour by the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's 21 km comparator is the original booked optimal for Blk 118 Rivervale Dr to Changi Terminal 1 - a routing that was never driven after her amendments. The trip_record's optimal_route_source records a re-quote at 07:41 after both endpoint amendments, and amended_optimal_distance_km is the stored 24.6. Under POL-RD-05 that stored amended figure, not the booked figure, is the baseline, so the '26.2 km versus 21 km' comparison the claim rests on uses the wrong comparator.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern can be built against this driver. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 402 - below both POL-RD-06 thresholds (3 or more flags, or a ratio of 0.05 with at least 40 completed trips) - so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check yields nothing adverse, and on the amended baseline the deviation is not MATERIAL in any event (6.4% is far below the 50% materiality figure and 1.57 km is far below 8.0 km).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-08 puts the initial burden on the rider to show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired gps_trace. This trace is unimpaired on its own terms - 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, a steady 10-second sampling interval - but once the amended baseline of 24.6 km is applied there is no qualifying excess at all, so the rider has not discharged her initial burden and no exculpatory clause even needs to be reached.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is nothing to correct on the pass-through side under POL-RD-09: erp_gantries is empty and tolls/ERP are 0.00, and the airport surcharge line is 0.00, which is correct because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there. No off-route gantry refund and no billing-integrity correction arises on this fare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.erp_gantries",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With no deviation surviving the amended-endpoint recomputation and no pass-through correction due, the POL-RD-02 optimal-route fare recomputation is never reached and the charged total of $33.77 stands. On a rider-filed dispute, NO_ACTION leaves payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 exactly as they are, which is the party-relative outcome POL-GEN-03 prescribes where the filing party's claim is not supported by the evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-05", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.total_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This is a rider-filed route-deviation dispute over a $33.77 fare for trip TRP-00108. Both parties' accounts agree on the decisive fact: the endpoints of this trip were changed after booking. The rider's own messages show the pin moved to Punggol MRT at 07:11:58 (pickup_amended_at 07:12:30) and the destination changed from Changi Terminal 1 to Terminal 3 at 07:41:40 (dropoff_amended_at 07:41:52), and the driver acknowledged each change. Under POL-RD-05, where the pickup or dropoff point is amended after booking - expressly including a T1-to-T3 terminal change - the deviation comparison must be re-run against the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints, which the platform stored as amended_optimal_distance_km 24.6 km (duration 31.0 min). The rider's 'usually 21 km' comparator is the original Blk 118 Rivervale-to-T1 booking, a route that was never driven after her two changes, and it cannot be the baseline.\n\nThe governing distance is the GPS polyline, trace_distance_km 26.17 km; under POL-RD-01 the trip_record's 26.2 km is a rounded convenience copy that may not be cited for the threshold test. Against the amended 24.6 km baseline the excess is 26.17 - 24.6 = 1.57 km, about 6.4% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to clear BOTH limits - greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km - and the percentage limb fails by a wide margin (6.4% against 20%). No deviation is established, and POL-RD-05 directs NO_ACTION where none survives the recomputation.\n\nBecause no deviation is established, the POL-RD-02 optimal-route recomputation is never reached. The recomputed fare of $27.63 and the resulting $6.15 refund the rider seeks arise only on the 21.0 km booking baseline, which does not apply, so the rider's request to measure the threshold on the booked itinerary is rejected. The charged total of $33.77 stands; on a rider-filed dispute, NO_ACTION leaves payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd $0.00 exactly as they are, as POL-GEN-03 provides.\n\nThe rider's account of the driver circling the airport for five minutes does not change this. Even taken entirely at face value it could only reduce distance further, and the whole trip already came in just 1.57 km over the re-quoted optimal for the amended endpoints - below the threshold at which any refund arises. The driver's alternative explanations were not needed: POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing here because the only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00108-01) carries no payload, and POL-RD-04 cannot be run because every chat message carries a null waypoint_hint, so its corroboration test is undecidable on this record and the case is decided on the remaining clauses.\n\nOn the pass-through side there is nothing to correct: no ERP gantries were charged and the airport surcharge is $0.00, which is correct because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there. No repeat-deviation pattern exists against the driver (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 402 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06 conduct referral is produced, and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity line exists. No driver compensation is due either: the distance charged (26.2 km) is not below the trace distance (26.17 km), so there is no unbilled shortfall exceeding 1.0 km under POL-RD-04. The trace is unimpaired on its own terms - 100% coverage, no gaps, a steady 10-second sampling interval - so no POL-RD-07 escalation arises. Finally, the rider's profile has not been used against her: deviation_claims_60d 1 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0 are below the POL-RD-08 thresholds, and the remaining profile fields are context only under POL-GEN-01.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. The $33.77 charge stands; nothing is refunded to the rider and nothing is paid to the driver."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

