    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties — this dispute ends with NO_ACTION: the $33.77 charged stands and neither a refund nor a driver payment is due.\n\nBoth endpoints of this ride were changed after booking, and both of you agree on that. The rider moved the pin to Punggol MRT at 07:12:30 and changed the destination to Changi Terminal 3 at 07:41:52 (chat messages at those times). POL-RD-05 therefore fixes the comparison at the amended optimal route of 24.6 km stored on the trip record (trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km), not the 21.0 km Rivervale-to-Terminal 1 route that was booked and never actually driven. The rider's 'this exact trip is 21 km' comparator is the wrong baseline; the 24.6 km re-quote is the stored field POL-RD-05 requires and no substitute may be derived.\n\nThe distance driven is read from the GPS polyline: 26.17 km (gps_trace.trace_distance_km). The receipt's 26.2 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement and may not be used for the test. Against the amended 24.6 km the excess is 1.57 km, about 6.4% of optimal. POL-RD-01 sets two gates that must BOTH be cleared — more than 0.8 km absolute AND more than 20% of optimal. The absolute figure clears the 0.8 km gate, but the percentage limb fails badly (6.4% is far below 20%), so no deviation is established and the POL-RD-02 recomputation is never reached. The rider's complaint about the driver circling the airport does not help her: whatever circling occurred is already inside the 26.17 km figure, and POL-RD-05's circling exclusion would if anything shrink the excess. The residual 1.57 km reflects the amended Punggol-to-T3 routing the rider herself requested, not an unexplained detour.\n\nBecause no deviation is established, no exculpatory clause needs to be reached. For completeness: the traffic advisory on file (EV-ADVIS-00108-01) carries no payload and exonerates nothing, and the rider-requested-detour test in POL-RD-04 cannot be run because no chat message carries a waypoint_hint or names a road (the clause says so itself) — neither point changes the outcome.\n\nNothing is due on the pass-through side. Tolls/ERP are 0.00 and erp_gantries is empty, and the airport surcharge is correctly 0.00 because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there, so there is no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4). No driver compensation is due either: the billed distance (26.2 km) is not less than the trace distance (26.17 km), so there is no unbilled shortfall under POL-RD-04.\n\nNo repeat-deviation pattern exists (deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 402 completed trips in 90 days), so no POL-RD-06 conduct referral issues. The rider's profile was not used against her. The disputed charge of $33.77 stands; payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 are left exactly as they are."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
